(7649997, 1244114, 167587, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mariuca:</b></div><hr/><i> Oh, and I see that you shoot with Fuji and with a 35 mm lens. I have the lighter weight one and am thrilled with it. What a sensor! <br/>Your pp, if any, was perfect. A splendid image. I voted a few seconds from midnight here and did not have time to go over and bump to 10 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, I shoot with both Fuji and Sony. I really like the Fuji X series and have the original X100, the X100F and the X-T3. Easy and great carry around cameras. Beautiful colors and good film simulations!<br/>My Sony is the A99ii, an A-Mount Full Frame, with big lenses. A very good camera, but a different beast altogether.<br/> <br/>Thank you for looking, and thanks for the comments.</td>', 'Originally posted by mariuca: Oh, and I see that you shoot with Fuji and with a 35 mm lens. I have the lighter weight one and am thrilled with it. What a sensor! Your pp, if any, was perfect. A splendid image. I voted a few seconds from midnight here and did not have time to go over and bump to 10   Yes, I shoot with both Fuji and Sony. I really like the Fuji X series and have the original X100, the X100F and the X-T3. Easy and great carry around cameras. Beautiful colors and good film simulations!My Sony is the A99ii, an A-Mount Full Frame, with big lenses. A very good camera, but a different beast altogether. Thank you for looking, and thanks for the comments.', '2020-01-08 21:35:20.000000', NULL, 0),
